{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>When any man of you offers.</b> When he offers from himself — with verbal confession and humility, in the manner of וּנְשַׁלְּמָה פָרִים שְׂפָתֵינוּ (Hosea 14:3), and as it says: זִבְחֵי אֱלֹהִים רוּחַ נִשְׁבָּרָה (Psalms 51:19) — for there is no desire in fools who bring without prior humility. And the Sages, of blessed memory, said: מִכֶּם וְלֹא כֻלְּכֶם, לְהוֹצִיא אֶת הַמּוּמָר — 'of you' and not all of you, to exclude the apostate." "<b>From the animals.</b> If he offers an animal, it may only be from cattle or sheep, not any species of wild animal, even though it falls under the category of behemah, as it says: זֹאת הַבְּהֵמָה אֲשֶׁר תֹּאכֵלוּ… אַיָּל וּצְבִי… (Deuteronomy 14:4–5). The purpose of these sections is to clarify the types of those who may bring offerings, the types of things offered, the types of offerings, and the reasons for offering them. He explained that freewill offerings are accepted from anyone, even from the nations, as he clarifies further on: וּמִיַּד בֶּן נֵכָר לֹא תַקְרִיבוּ אֶת לֶחֶם אֱלֹהֵיכֶם מִכָּל אֵלֶּה כִּי מָשְׁחָתָם בָּהֶם מוּם בָּם (Leviticus 22:25) — and apostates are inferior to the nations, all the more so apostates to idolatry and to public Sabbath desecration. He explained that the types of things offered are cattle and sheep among animals, turtledoves and pigeons among birds, and fine flour, oil, and frankincense. He explained that the types of offerings from them include burnt offering, peace offering, and meal offering — which sometimes come as freewill gifts — and from them sin offering and guilt offering, which come only as obligations. From this the matter of Cain is clarified: וְאֶל קַיִן וְאֶל מִנְחָתוֹ לֹא שָׁעָה (Genesis 4:5) — for he was of the class of heretics from whom offerings are not accepted, as his end proved concerning his beginning, and his meal offering was of a type unfit for the altar. So too with Noah: וַיָּרַח ה׳ אֶת רֵיחַ הַנִּיחֹחַ (Genesis 8:21) — he accepted that portion of his offerings which was fit for a pleasing fragrance, being of a type fit for the altar, but he did not accept his entire offering, which was from every clean animal and every clean bird. One may also understand what he intended in saying זֶבַח וּמִנְחָה לֹא חָפַצְתָּ אָזְנַיִם כָּרִיתָ לִּי (Psalms 40:7), and לָמָּה לִּי רֹב זִבְחֵיכֶם (Isaiah 1:11), and many similar verses in the holy books. For indeed it is fitting that the one bringing the offering be a qualified person, choosing a type fit for sacrifice, suited to achieve the end for whose sake he comes to bring it, and he shall lean his hand upon his offering as one submitting and praying that his iniquity be placed upon the head of the offering — like the matter of the scapegoat — and thereby he brings into actual effect the intent of repentance that is in his heart, and it is accepted to make atonement upon him. And since the species of sin are partly in thought of the heart alone and partly also in deed, to atone for the heart's thought that portion which goes up in the flame of the altar is fitting — these are the burnt offering and the parts of offerings that go up in smoke and the memorial portion of meal offerings — while to atone for the deed the portions of the offering given to the priests are fitting. This is the exchange for the limbs of the sinner: that he who engaged in the activity of evil gives the limbs of the offering to the servants of El who engage in His service, as it says: וְאוֹתָהּ נָתַן לָכֶם לָשֵׂאת אֶת עֲוֹן הָעֵדָה לְכַפֵּר עֲלֵיהֶם (Leviticus 10:17); and so the Sages of blessed memory said: the priests eat and the owners achieve atonement. And since the evil act requiring atonement by offering is partly severe in iniquity — such as those liable to excision — and partly lighter than this but involving some profanation of the sacred, for the first category the sin offering is fitting, to purify the soul that became defiled through liability to excision, as it says: וְנִכְרְתָה הַנֶּפֶשׁ הַהִיא (Leviticus 7:20); and for the second category the guilt offering is fitting, to remove the profanation for which he has incurred guilt — and this is through the humility of the offering together with repentance, and one law applies to them both. The peace offering, however, is as though the owners join with the ministers of El to serve Him shoulder to shoulder. And since sinners stand on different levels — some prone to stumble in sin and others far from this, in whom it occurs only rarely — Scripture speaks of them in varying ways and their offerings vary. Therefore concerning the anointed priest, because he is far from stumbling in sin, he said:"], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:36:00.972021139Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}